> when he has the time, he might do it.
>
> Doing anything beyond merely uploading them, any kind of special handling,
> would require even more time and effort.
>
> Messing with jbovlaste in any way is very low on Robin's priority list,
> especially considering his desire for jbovlaste 2.0 to be created to replace
> it.
>
> Conclusion: Robin might, /might/, at some time in the future upload all the
> ISO words to jbovlaste. But nothing more. But more likely, najrut will have
> to put them on there himself if he wants them there this year.
>
>
>
>
> As to the words themselves, my reason for not wanting them is because when
> it comes to all or nothing situations, I prefer nothing. The conversation
> that spawned those two huge lists was about the cultural gismu, and the fact
> that some cultures had a gismu, whereas others did not, and that this was an
> example of Lojban /not/ being culturally neutral. It was decided that the
> only way to be culturally neutral was either for all cultures to have there
> own words, which resulted in a huge list of words based on ISO codes of
> counrties and languages, or for none to have their own word, which resulted
> in the creation of this list:
